"D-164 serving-read evidence now has one five-field optional nullable contract shared by ObservationReport and NodeDetail. Revision 15/API 1.11.0 keeps all 50 operations and absent/null/value compatibility, including the canonical hashes of six old observation fixtures. It also aligns the existing D-112 default-bound and D-117 finite-grant documentation/vectors with their adopted behavior.\n\nThe historical-input migration preserves six exact frozen inputs and all 42 previous handover claim bodies. The secops index changes exactly 120 digest scalars across seven paths. This merge provides the schema/generated compatibility phase; Central persistence/projection, diagnostic consumers and producer rollout remain separate owner work. F17-01/D-163 remains open.\n\nIndependent orchestrator verification of integrated head 06fc1197b7f7007943d3f01b997a107f6e13ced1 (main 6520a312 plus native 2d5205bf and serialization correction 60e0a401): all passed under the orchestrator reservation. Verification covered contracts-verify (including 201 TS checks), secops tests, committed netlab/e2e evidence, full Go unit and database integration suites, both architecture builds, formatting/vet/lint, all domain lints and generated drift, clean tree, scope and diff hygiene. Static review independently verified all six archived source inputs, the 42 old claim bodies and 120 hash-only index replacements. Native development failures and final passing receipts are disclosed below.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Native test source commit:** `2d5205bf3f7e9962a1775009ce12e6f61fe62dfe` on branch `w3-contracts-r13`, based on `BASE_HEAD = 980e313ab8d1b261cb1f44e4a86b54b7e55fefde` (handover follow-up 48 PR `#483`, merged at `2026-11-05T06:23:33Z`, merge commit `ff0ce0658b9a86523bd6bc2ddf1fceda47a5453f`, cut commit `b921c75f180beb6c0051d585a86d6651b2c8d71a`). API version advances to **`1.11.0`**, contract revision **15**, operation count unchanged at **50** (`0` operations added, removed, or renamed). Commit trailer: `Agent: agy/gemini-4-argon-high`.\n- **Serialization correction commit:** `60e0a4012c0ed942c3402cb1992fcc06a6592787` (`contracts: restore scope-review.json Unicode escape formatting in revision 15`, trailer `Agent: agy/gemini-4-argon-high`), recorded separately from native test source `2d5205bf3f7e9962a1775009ce12e6f61fe62dfe`. This single-file tracked commit restores the original `980e313ab8d1b261cb1f44e4a86b54b7e55fefde` Unicode escape spelling (`\\u00a7`, `\\u2013`, etc.) on 33 unrelated lines in `docs/e2e/at/secops/scope-review.json` while preserving the exact 120 `sha256` scalar updates across the 7 changed paths (parsed JSON is identical to `2d5205bf:docs/e2e/at/secops/scope-review.json`, and raw bytes match `980e313a:docs/e2e/at/secops/scope-review.json` outside the 120 updated `sha256` lines).\n\nDuring an earlier pass, the orchestrator interrupted the wrapper after read-only inspection found three D-164 departures in the in-progress draft (an invented `error_code` property on `ServingReadEvidence`, a claim that `verified=true` clears `diagnostic` to `\"\"`, and `NodeDetail.serving_read` wording that did not scope `null` and ETag updates to the selected current-incarnation observation). That orchestrator design interruption is separate from the five initial `contracts-verify` test/lint failures disclosed under Self-check results below. All three design departures were corrected before regeneration and final verification:\n\n1. **D-164 (`ServingReadEvidence`, `ObservationReport.serving_read`, `NodeDetail.serving_read`):**\n   - Added shared component `ServingReadEvidence` with `additionalProperties: false` and the **exact five required members** (`read_at`, `source`, `candidate_generation`, `verified`, `diagnostic`) and no `error_code` property.\n   - Referenced by optional nullable `ObservationReport.serving_read` and optional nullable `NodeDetail.serving_read` (`x-omitempty: false`, `x-omitzero: true`, generated as `presence.Nullable[ServingReadEvidence]`). Only those two entries were added to `TestAPI01_OptionalNullableFields` in `contracts/openapi_test.go`.\n   - `read_at` is the actual UTC RFC 3339 (`Z`) time of the last complete `VerifyServing` read (never refreshed on later heartbeats without a new read; may be older than `observed_at` and is not required to be `<= observed_at`). `source` is `apply` or `live`. `candidate_generation` is a `decstr.U64` decimal string (`^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$`, `maxLength: 20`) naming the candidate generation under verification, never an applied-generation ACK. `verified` is the complete `VerifyServing` outcome (`false` is a meaningful rejected read, not omission).\n   - `diagnostic` (`maxLength: 500`) carries the producer's bounded/redacted string (`read_at=… source=… candidate=… verified=… ` plus `Evidence.ReportDetail()`, clipped to the first 500 bytes by `clipMsg`) as opaque text for **both** `verified=true` and `verified=false`, matching `node/agent/serving_evidence.go` (`attachServingRead`) and `node/agent/meterreset.go` (`clipMsg`).\n   - On `NodeDetail.serving_read`, absent means the server does not project the field yet (pre-revision-15) and `null` means the selected current-incarnation observation has no available `serving_read` (not that no earlier read was ever reported in that incarnation; servers do not search back for a last non-null read). It shares existing selected-observation and strong-ETag (`resource_version`) semantics without claiming that accepting any observation increments `nodes.resource_version` (`internal/nodes/observations.go` updates node state only inside `isNewerOrEqual`).\n   - All six existing `ObservationReport` fixtures (`ObservationReport.json`, `ObservationReport.awaiting-member-grants.json`, `ObservationReport.tc-verified.json`, `ObservationReport.tc-rejected.json`, `ObservationReport.tc-truncated.json`, `ObservationReport.tc-null.json`) remain byte-for-byte unchanged and keep their exact canonical JCS and raw SHA-256 digests.\n2. **D-112 (`submitUsageBatch` and `UsageBatchRequest.origin_incarnation_id` wording):**\n   - Live descriptions in `contracts/openapi.yaml` and `docs/contracts/README.md` state that a handed-off event's `interval_end` is bounded by `retired_at` plus the Central configured bound `sampling_interval_bound_seconds` (`UsageBatchConfig.SamplingIntervalBound`, default **10 seconds**; Central stores no per-stream historical sampling interval), removing the legacy phrase `\"in force for the retired stream\"`.\n   - `contracts/vectors/usage-retired-handoff.json` preserves `sampling_interval_seconds: 30` and all request/response bytes intact while adding `sampling_interval_bound_default_seconds: 10` and clarifying in `_comment` that `30` is that vector scenario's Central bound override.\n3. **D-117 (`revokeMemberGrant` finite-grant correction):**\n   - Live `revokeMemberGrant` description in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, `docs/contracts/README.md`, and `contracts/revision14_test.go` state that all entitlement grants are finite (`valid_until` is `NOT NULL` and `isfinite`) and open-ended grant creation remains forbidden.\n   - Removed the obsolete `open-ended` case from `contracts/internal/gen/revision14.go` and regenerated `contracts/vectors/member-grant-revoke.json` (retaining `finite`, `same-key-replay`, `unknown-or-other-member`, `already-revoked`, `expired`).\n4. **One-time Handover Compatibility Migration:**\n   - Updated the five current contract-version/revision sentences in `docs/handover/README.md`, `docs/handover/operator-guide.md`, `docs/handover/member-guide.md`, and `docs/ops/README.md` to revision 15 / OpenAPI `1.11.0` / 50 operations.\n   - Added frozen revision-14 and pre-migration snapshots plus `provenance.json` under `tests/handover/testdata/history/contracts-revision-15/`, reusing existing `tests/handover/testdata/history/follow-up-15/operator-guide.md` (`982c209e3f1fb6603138e0bc2a6ee4a5191b4e89:docs/handover/operator-guide.md`, 203,771 bytes, SHA-256 `061b72db8c6d235d914de357